      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Fibo 2 Edit Turbo\n\n1. Upload an image.\n2. Set **Scale**: **1** = input size, **0.5** = half width/height, **2** = double width/height.\n3. Optionally enter **width** and **height** in **Resolution override**.\n4. Describe the edit and Run.\n\n**Width 0 + height 0:** use Scale.\n**Both dimensions set:** use that resolution instead of Scale.\n**Only one set:** calculate the other from the input aspect ratio.\n\nExample: width **1024**, height **1024** restores the original square output size. Leave the override's method and crop settings at their defaults; it calculates dimensions only. Fibo always receives the original uploaded image.\n\nFibo rounds dimensions down to multiples of 16. A changed aspect ratio center-crops the reference for the requested output. Larger resolutions use more GPU memory.\n\nDefaults: scale **1**, override **0 \u00d7 0**, **4 steps**, **CFG 1**, Euler / simple. No prompt-enhancer or external API dependency.\n\nFibo weights \u00a9 BRIA AI, **CC BY-NC 4.0**; commercial use requires a separate Bria agreement. Derived from Comfy Org's MIT-licensed template. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt."
      ]
    },
